{
  "method": "Finite exact deformed Human surface analysis with unchanged >65% digit ownership and noncoplanar edge/triangle crossing rules. Bidirectional sample-to-nearest target patch distance uses geometric outward triangle winding. Negative signed distances count as strong local inside evidence only when nearest projection lies strictly inside its face (barycentric >1e-6) and the open target patch generalized winding number is >=0.75. Vertices and centroids across each patch, grid-8 barycentric samples on every intersecting triangle, and near-intersection-to-vertex fractions 0.001/0.003/0.01/0.03/0.1/0.25/0.5 are included. Extents refer to crossing curve points, and intersected triangle area includes whole faces, not overlap area.",
  "limitations": [
    "Signed nearest-patch values are sampled local separations, not exact maximum solid penetration, minimum separating translation, overlap volume, or clinical anatomy.",
    "The supplementary at-least-1-mm-from-both-boundaries statistic is a sensitivity descriptor, not a clearance gate. A zero value with zero retained samples is inconclusive and never removes the full boundary-inclusive distance or crossing failure.",
    "Finger ownership patches are open at the web/base; the winding threshold is a local confidence filter, not watertight solid containment. Excluded boundary and inconclusive orientation counts remain visible.",
    "Finite samples may underestimate deepest intrusion, particularly tiny slivers; raw intersection counts remain failure evidence regardless of distance.",
    "Noncoplanar method retains the incumbent omissions for coplanar contact, mixed-web patch crossings and entirely enclosed surfaces.",
    "Selected cases represent owner-reported residuals plus broad baseline controls. No timing window, full score clearance, key gate or final visual approval is established."
  ],
